02"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Fig. 3</label><caption><p>CD44std immunohistochemical staining shows strong positive along the cytoplasmic membrane in DCIS (A) and negative in invasive ductal carcinoma (B)(&#x000d7; 200).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-47-333-g003"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Expression of MMP and TIMP mRNAs, CD44std, and Angiogenic Factors in Ductal Carcinoma <italic>in Situ</italic> (DCIS) and Invasive Ductal Carcinoma (IDC) of the Breast</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-47-333-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05; NS, not significant.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Expression levels of MMP and TIMP mRNAs and CD44std with Clinical Prognostic Parameters of the Breast Carcinoma</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-47-333-i002"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>HG, histologic grade; NG, nuclear grade.</p><p><sup>*</sup><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05; NS, not significant.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Microvessel Density and Expression of Angiogenic Factors with Clinical Prognostic Parameters of the Breast Carcinoma</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-47-333-i003"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>HG, histologic grade; NG, nuclear grade.</p><p><sup>*</sup><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05; NS, not significant.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Correlation of MT1-MMP mRNA and TIMP2 mRNA Expression Levels in Invasive Ductal Carcinoma</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-47-333-i004"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p><sup>*</sup><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>